{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Compare Bitcoin accumulation with cash savings"},"description":"Illustrates how a lump sum plus monthly contributions might grow in Bitcoin compared with cash savings, nominal and after inflation. Deterministic; the same model as the live Bitcoin Accumulation Calculator. Bitcoin grows on a smooth path at bitcoinCagrPct (0 to 100), an illustrative assumption chosen by the caller, never a forecast; above 45% the result carries the page's stress-testing advisory. Presets: conservative (Bitcoin 12%, cash 3%, inflation 3%), base (Bitcoin 20%, cash 2%, inflation 3%), aggressive (Bitcoin 45%, cash 2%, inflation 3%), bear (Bitcoin 0%, cash 2%, inflation 5%); explicit rates override the preset. Omitted values take the page's starting values (initialAmount 10000, monthlyContribution 500, years 10); A negative or non-finite years value is rejected. Years above 50 are clamped as the page clamps them, as are other out-of-range values, and the result echoes what was used. Currency USD, EUR, GBP, AUD or JPY, in either letter case. btcPrice is a starting price in that currency supplied by the caller (with USD, btcPriceUsd is accepted as an alias). Without it the server's cached market reference is used, labelled live, or a fixed illustrative price when that reference is unavailable. The illustrative price is not a market quotation. The price sets the BTC amounts only; the value comparison does not depend on it. No fees, no tax. It does not assess suitability and recommends no amount or allocation.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"bitcoinCagrPct":{"type":"number"},"btcPrice":{"exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"btcPriceUsd":{"deprecated":true,"description":"Alias of btcPrice, in USD.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"currency":{"enum":["USD","EUR","GBP","AUD","JPY","usd","eur","gb